  "id": "COMPOUND:19836 - PROTEIN:2641",
  "verbalization": "Ardisiamamilloside F appears to be a potent inhibitor of EDD domain protein, DegV family members through a multi-step mechanism involving protein kinase C eta. The compound targets protein kinase C eta, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including 2-(4-Methyl-5-oxocyclohex-3-en-1-yl)propan-2-yl acetate, (2Z,5Z,8Z)-Tetradeca-2,5,8-Trien-1-Ol, and Triethylhexanoin. All of these compounds are known to interact with the EDD domain protein, DegV family, suggesting a common pathway of action. The evidence indicates that Ardisiamamilloside F may exert its effects by modulating protein kinase C eta, which then leads to the activation or inhibition of the EDD domain protein, DegV family. This relationship is supported by the consistent targeting of protein kinase C eta as a key intermediate in the pathway, highlighting a potential role for this kinase in the downstream effects of Ardisiamamilloside F. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of multiple compounds with similar targets, suggesting a broader pharmacological profile.",
